A listing's field mapping can map the site's own catalog columns: a mapping field that names a vocabulary (`vocabulary: { '@id': 'plone.app.vocabularies.MetadataFields' }` beside `sourceFields`) offers each of its columns too, as text, skipping one that repeats a declared source in another case. Block sanity accepts the same columns. The default listing schema names MetadataFields; a frontend that declares its own listing names it on its own mapping field.
